## Known Limitations

| Limitation | Scope |
|---|---|
| **No real auth** | Session persisted via `localStorage` per role; phone‑OTP sign‑in not yet integrated. |
| **No consent revocation UI for workers** | Only the mother can withdraw; worker cannot unilaterally revoke. |
| **Milestone names are placeholders** | `[PLACEHOLDER] Registration`, etc. — final wording to come from clinical lead. |
| **No D1/R2 production bindings** | All data lives in local Firestore emulator only; deploy requires Sites config. |
| **No offline / push / QR / voice** | As requested — skipped for this demo. |
| **No audit‑trail edit protection beyond versioning** | Earlier versions visible via disclosure triangle; edit keeps history. |
| **Language switcher writes to localStorage only** | Shared across roles via per‑device storage; not synced to backend. |
| **Single mother demo dataset** | 3 seed mothers but flow validated end‑to‑end with Savitri/Anita/Pooja patterns. |
| **Handover revocation fully removes Village B access** | Verified: after step 10, Village B "Incoming mothers" list is empty; card is read‑only. |

