## Quick Run‑Through (5 lines or fewer)

```bash
# 1. Start local emulators
npm run emulators

# 2. Seed synthetic data
npm run seed

# 3. Dev server (Vite + PWA)
npm run dev          # → http://localhost:5173

# 4. Demo the flow
#    - ASHA logs in → mother list → journey card → milestone + visit
#    - "Mother is moving" → consent → handover pending
#    - ANM in Village B → incoming → Accept → add visits
#    - Mother view → withdraw consent → revoked, back to Village A

# 5. Typecheck + build pass
npx tsc --noEmit && npm run build   # ✅ exit 0
```

All 10 steps connect through a **single shared Firestore + emulator data layer**, with audit trails on every write, role‑gated access, and multilingual text from the EN/HI/MR JSON files. No real patient data is ever used — everything is synthetic.

